From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Jul 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WASM: symmetric headless fast path for setComponent DETACH (BUG-20)

Root cause of the shutdown_office() trap ("function signature mismatch", every
instance, since forever — BUG-20):

lo_destroy() -> Desktop::terminate() -> impl_closeFrames() -> XFrameImpl::close()
-> setComponent(nullptr, nullptr).  The stock detach path broadcasts
FrameAction_COMPONENT_DETACHING.  The frame's TitleHelper reacts
(frameAction -> impl_updateListeningForFrame -> impl_setSubTitle) and calls
SfxBaseController::addTitleChangeListener on the dying headless controller,
whose impl_getTitleHelper() lazily creates a NEW framework::TitleHelper for a
controller that is seconds from disposal, with a model that is already closed.
That helper self-registers into the controller's m_aListenerContainer from
inside its own constructor, and construction-time Reference temporaries drive
its refcount to zero before impl_getTitleHelper() returns: measured via CDP
wasm breakpoints — cppu::OWeakObject::release() fires twice from inside the
TitleHelper constructor call chain and dlfree(helper) is reached from within
SfxBaseController::impl_getTitleHelper() itself, with no ~TitleHelper frame
(inlined) and no removeEventListener ever called.  The controller's listener
container is left holding a raw pointer to freed memory (acquired via
addInterface, never released).  SfxBaseController::dispose() then iterates the
container; OInterfaceIteratorHelper2's constructor virtual-calls acquire()
through the freed object's clobbered vtable, and under WASM that call_indirect
deterministically traps with "function signature mismatch", aborting
lo_destroy() before any teardown or static reset runs.

The attach side of setComponent already takes a headless fast path (patch
20251221_210000) that skips implts_sendFrameActionEvent(COMPONENT_ATTACHED) —
so frame listeners were never introduced to the headless controller in the
first place.  Broadcasting COMPONENT_DETACHING at teardown is therefore
asymmetric, and it is exactly what wakes the TitleHelper chain.  Fix: mirror
the attach fast path on the detach side.  When LOK-headless (EMSCRIPTEN + LOK
active), both arguments are null and the frame has no component window, skip
window listening/broadcast work entirely: clear m_xController and protocol
handlers under the SolarMutex, dispose the old controller, and return.  The
controller's dispose() still runs (its listener container is now empty, so no
trap), close() then proceeds to dispose the frame, and lo_destroy() finally
reaches Application::Quit, the LibLibreOffice_Impl delete, and the extended
static reset (which had never executed before this fix).

diff --git a/framework/source/services/frame.cxx b/framework/source/services/frame.cxx
--- a/framework/source/services/frame.cxx
+++ b/framework/source/services/frame.cxx
@@ -1463,6 +1463,55 @@
         return true;
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // WASM/LOK headless mode: symmetric fast path for DETACH (BUG-20).
+    // The attach fast path above never broadcast COMPONENT_ATTACHED, so frame
+    // listeners were never introduced to the headless controller.  The stock
+    // detach path below would broadcast COMPONENT_DETACHING anyway, which makes
+    // the frame's TitleHelper poke the dying controller
+    // (SfxBaseController::addTitleChangeListener -> impl_getTitleHelper),
+    // spawning a TitleHelper that is freed during construction-time reentrancy
+    // while the controller's listener container still holds its raw pointer.
+    // SfxBaseController::dispose() then virtual-calls acquire() through freed
+    // memory and traps ("function signature mismatch"), aborting lo_destroy().
+    // Skip the UI broadcasts entirely and just dispose the controller: headless
+    // conversion has no UI listeners that need COMPONENT_DETACHING.
+    if (comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive()
+        && !xController.is() && !xComponentWindow.is()
+        && !m_xComponentWindow.is())
+    {
+        std::cerr << "[FRAME] LOK headless mode: fast path for setComponent detach" << std::endl << std::flush;
+        checkDisposed();
+        css::uno::Reference< css::frame::XController > xOldController;
+        /* SAFE { */
+        {
+            SolarMutexGuard aWriteLock;
+            xOldController = m_xController;
+            m_xController.clear();
+            if (m_xDispatchHelper)
+            {
+                rtl::Reference<DispatchProvider> pDispatchProvider = m_xDispatchHelper->GetSlave();
+                if (pDispatchProvider)
+                    pDispatchProvider->ClearProtocolHandlers();
+            }
+            m_bConnected = false;
+        }
+        /* } SAFE */
+        if (xOldController.is())
+        {
+            try
+            {
+                xOldController->dispose();
+            }
+            catch(const css::lang::DisposedException&)
+                {}
+        }
+        xOldController.clear();
+        std::cerr << "[FRAME] LOK headless setComponent detach completed" << std::endl << std::flush;
+        return true;
+    }
+#endif
+
     checkDisposed();
 
     // Get threadsafe some copies of used members.
